"""Generate an interactive HTML keymap viewer from a QMK keymap.

Tier-4 of the keymap visualization: a self-contained HTML page with layer tabs,
hover tooltips, a light/dark theme, and the F15 combo mode (role dots, accent
glyph badges on the keys, and a chord panel) — everything derived from the
keymap sources (keymap.c, custom_keycodes.h, combos.c, custom_functions.c).

Reads only — never writes into the keymap's directory. Output goes to
<userspace>/viz/<keyboard>/<keymap>/keymap.html by default.

Only external requirement: the `qmk` CLI with your QMK_HOME configured.

Usage:
  ./tools/keymap-html -kb <keyboard> -km <keymap> [-o <outfile>] [--layout LAYOUT_foo]
                      [--halcyon-modules] [--triggers KC_X:accent ...]

Example:
  ./tools/keymap-html -kb splitkb/halcyon/elora -km colemakdh_hlc
"""

